{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1069","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1069","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1069\",\"parent_revision\":\"21260107f7ab0a9f10e584909311915cff1029c225df8d21b74f712fe5923886\",\"root_revision\":\"21260107f7ab0a9f10e584909311915cff1029c225df8d21b74f712fe5923886\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen the orchestrator spawns teams via TeamCreate and the session hits context compaction, all awareness of the running teams is lost. After compaction the orchestrator ignores the still-running teammates \u2014 they complete or idle with no follow-up, and the session ends with orphaned agents.\\n\\nObserved: 9 teammates left running in vm-flightsimulator session after compaction. Orchestrator did not wait for results, did not send shutdown, did not resume.\\n\\nRoot cause: No mechanism persists active team state before compaction or restores it after. The kage-bunshin hooks handle subprocess notifications but not team-level orchestration state.\\n\\nRequired fix (two parts):\\n1. Persist active team state (team IDs, teammate names, task summaries) to a file before or during compaction \u2014 candidate: PreCompact hook writing to ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/active-teams.json\\n2. Restore orchestrator awareness after compaction \u2014 candidate: PostCompact or SessionStart hook injecting a prompt reminder listing the active teams and their tasks, so the orchestrator picks up where it left off\\n\\nThe compact instructions in CLAUDE.md are insufficient on their own \u2014 the orchestrator needs a structural reminder injected at the hook level, not just guidelines it may not have context to apply.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAIM 1: \\\"#1071 must ship first \u2014 beads must be installed and initialized before this workflow can write state to it\\\"\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: GitHub issue #1071 status check\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-24\\n  - Command: gh issue view 1071 -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills --json state\\n  - Result: {\\\"number\\\":1071,\\\"state\\\":\\\"CLOSED\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"feat: feat: Auto-bootstrap beads in backlog MCP server lifespan startup\\\"}\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Git repository history via gh API\\n  - Finding: Issue #1071 is closed and marked as completed\\n\\nEXPLANATION: #1071 is closed and has completed. The dependency claim that \\\"#1071 must ship first\\\" is verified.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 2: \\\"`bd` is on PATH (guaranteed by #1071)\\\"\\n\\nVERDICT: REFUTED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: PATH check via `which` command\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-24\\n  - Command: which bd\\n  - Result: NOT_FOUND (command returned exit code 1, no path returned)\\n  - Command: bd --version\\n  - Result: UNAVAILABLE (/bin/bash: line 1: bd: command not found)\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Bash shell PATH search at execution time\\n  - Finding: bd is not available in the shell's PATH, despite #1071 being closed. #1071 may have provided bootstrap logic, but the current session does not have bd installed or on PATH.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Despite #1071 being closed, bd is NOT currently available on PATH. The guarantee claimed in the dependencies does not hold in the current environment.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 3: \\\"`TeammateIdle` hook event is confirmed available in Claude Code hooks docs\\\"\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-core-reference/SKILL.md, line 30\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-24\\n  - Content: |\\n      | `TeammateIdle`       | Agent team teammate about to go idle                         | No                                     | Quality gates           |\\n  - Additional source: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-guide/references/claude-code.md, line 43\\n  - Content: | `TeammateIdle` | When an agent team teammate is about to go idle | none |\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: hooks-core-reference SKILL.md table of all hook events (lines 16-45)\\n  - Finding: TeammateIdle is listed as a defined event with \\\"Quality gates\\\" as a common use case\\n\\nEXPLANATION: TeammateIdle is confirmed in the official Claude Code hooks documentation as an available hook event.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 4: \\\"PreCompact hook can write to ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/active-teams.json before compaction\\\"\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-core-reference/SKILL.md, line 36\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-24\\n  - Content: |\\n      | `PreCompact`         | Before context compaction                                    | Yes \u2014 `manual` or `auto`               | State backup            |\\n  - Additional source: hooks-guide/references/claude-code.md, lines 52, 96 and decision control table line 231\\n  - Content: PreCompact fires before compaction; decision control row shows \\\"PreCompact | None | No decision control\\\" but command hooks can execute any bash command\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Hook execution model per hooks-core-reference (line 386)\\n  - Finding: All command hooks run in cwd with Claude Code's environment. Hook type \\\"command\\\" can execute any bash script, including those that write files.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: PreCompact fires before context compaction and can execute command hooks that write files. The capability is confirmed.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 5: \\\"PostCompact or SessionStart hook can inject a prompt reminder to the orchestrator\\\"\\n\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY REFUTED (PostCompact cannot; SessionStart can)\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-guide/references/claude-code.md\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-24\\n  - PostCompact output handling (line 195): \\\"PostCompact | No | Logged to debug only\\\"\\n  - SessionStart output handling (line 388): \\\"SessionStart, Setup\\\" \u2192 \\\"Added to Claude's context\\\"\\n  - Decision control table (line 231): \\\"WorktreeRemove, Notification, SessionEnd, PreCompact | None | No decision control\\\"\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Event-specific output table spanning lines 388-401 of hooks-core-reference SKILL.md\\n  - Finding: PostCompact output is \\\"Logged to debug only (`--debug`)\\\" \u2014 explicitly NOT added to Claude's context. SessionStart output IS \\\"Added to Claude's context\\\".\\n\\nEXPLANATION: PostCompact cannot inject prompt content to the orchestrator (output is debug-only). SessionStart can. The claim conflates two different hooks; one capability exists (SessionStart), the other does not (PostCompact). The fix design should use SessionStart for prompt injection, not PostCompact.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 6: \\\"`bd prime` output at SessionStart lists the active teams \u2014 the orchestrator can read this\\\"\\n\\nVERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: bd CLI availability check\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-24\\n  - Command: which bd\\n  - Result: NOT_FOUND\\n  - Command: bd --version\\n  - Result: UNAVAILABLE\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Command execution in current environment\\n  - Finding: bd is not installed or on PATH in this session, so the behavior of `bd prime` cannot be verified. #1071 is closed, but bd is not present in the current execution environment.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Cannot verify the claim because bd is not available to test. The claim is about bd's runtime behavior, which requires bd to be installed and executable. Without bd on PATH, the behavior of `bd prime` cannot be confirmed or refuted from this environment.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  VERIFIED SOURCES:\\n  - plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-core-reference/SKILL.md (accessed 2026-04-24)\\n  - plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-guide/references/claude-code.md (accessed 2026-04-24)\\n  - GitHub issue #1071 state via `gh issue view 1071 -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills` (accessed 2026-04-24)\\n  - Command execution results for `which bd` and `bd --version` (2026-04-24)\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Implementation Gate: fix: Orchestrator loses active team state across context compaction\\nDate: 2026-05-23\\nGate: dh:rt-ica (blocking \u2014 implementation gate)\\nPrior: dh:planner-rt-ica returned APPROVED for planning (2026-04-24). This is a fresh blocking assessment.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 The hooks manifest is the sole registration point for all lifecycle hooks. Adding PreCompact and TeammateIdle event handlers requires new entries in this file. No PreCompact, PostCompact, or TeammateIdle hooks are currently present. | Risk: HIGH | Why: This file gates whether hook scripts fire at all; missing or malformed entries mean team state is never persisted regardless of the hook script quality.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs` \u2014 SessionStart hook that injects `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` into conversation context via `hookSpecificOutput`. If PostCompact or SessionStart is the chosen restoration mechanism, this file is the direct precedent for that pattern; a new hook must replicate its output mechanism. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: The `hookSpecificOutput` mechanism (used here for SessionStart) is the only confirmed path for injecting context into the conversation at hook time; PostCompact hook output is confirmed to emit only to stderr (no `hookSpecificOutput` support per RT-ICA condition 4), so a new hook injecting team state must use SessionStart or a different mechanism.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs` \u2014 Stop hook that reads the kage-bunshin registry and blocks the orchestrator when idle sessions exist. The active-teams state written by the new PreCompact hook must use a file path and schema consistent with what this and related hooks already read. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: If the new PreCompact hook writes to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/active-teams.json` but the Stop hook's idle-check pattern diverges from the same state source, restoration will be incomplete and the Stop hook may present stale or conflicting data.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 The primary skill that orchestrates team creation via `TeamCreate`. After spawning a team, this is where the `bd update` step (or equivalent) must be added to write active team state to beads on the current task. | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is the origination point for all `TeamCreate` invocations under this workflow; if no state-write step is added here after team creation, no state will be available to persist at compaction time.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` \u2014 The dispatch skill instructs orchestrators to use `TeamCreate` and `TeamDelete`. A TeammateIdle hook must complement the dispatch pattern for tracking when individual teammates finish. The `monitor.py` health check covers kage-bunshin sessions, not Claude Code native teams \u2014 that gap is part of this item's blast radius. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: The dispatch skill defines the team lifecycle the orchestrator follows; if the new hook pattern contradicts or supplements what dispatch.md teaches, agents will receive conflicting instructions.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs` \u2014 Consumes `registry-{session_id}.json` at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/kage-bunshin/`. If the new active-teams state lives at `state/active-teams.json`, this hook does not read it \u2014 but the Stop hook is the primary mechanism for blocking the orchestrator when sessions are idle. If compaction-restored awareness is injected at SessionStart and the Stop hook does not cross-reference it, restored sessions may pass through Stop without being noticed. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: The Stop hook is the gatekeeper for session cleanup; incomplete cross-referencing between the new team state file and the existing registry means the stop-hook safety net has a gap.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs` \u2014 TaskCompleted hook that reads the same kage-bunshin registry. Same cross-referencing concern: native Claude Code teams spawned via TeamCreate do not write to the kage-bunshin registry, so this hook will never surface them. The new TeammateIdle hook must handle the gap the task-completed hook cannot. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Current hook explicitly handles only kage-bunshin tmux sessions; native TeamCreate sessions are invisible to it, creating a systemic gap in idle-session detection.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-end-kage-bunshin-cleanup.cjs` \u2014 SessionEnd hook that kills tmux sessions in the registry. If native team sessions persist after compaction and this hook fires at SessionEnd, it will not clean them up (they are not in the kage-bunshin registry). Orphaned native team sessions after SessionEnd remain unaddressed by this hook. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Cleanup gap for native TeamCreate sessions \u2014 SessionEnd will not kill them regardless of what the new PreCompact hook writes.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 PostToolUse and SubagentStop hook that tracks SAM task context via `active-task-{session_id}.json`. This hook uses `dh_paths.context_dir()` as the state directory. A PreCompact hook writing to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/active-teams.json` uses a different subdirectory (`state/`) that `dh_paths` does not currently have an accessor for. | Risk: LOW | Why: The file itself will not break, but it defines the precedent state layout \u2014 the new hook must follow or extend the same `dh_paths` pattern to stay consistent.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` \u2014 Provides path resolution for all DH state directories. The new hook needs a `state_dir()` function (or reuse of an existing path) to resolve `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/`. If the new hook hardcodes the path rather than using `dh_paths`, the `DH_STATE_HOME` override will be ignored. | Risk: HIGH | Why: All existing hooks that persist state use `dh_paths` or re-implement its slug derivation via `git rev-parse`. If the new PreCompact hook and its consuming SessionStart hook do not honor `DH_STATE_HOME`, tests and CI that set that override will break.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py` \u2014 SQLite dispatch state for milestone waves. Schema has no team/teammate columns: only `milestone`, `wave_num`, `issue`, `title`, `status`, `pid`, timestamps, `result`, `error`, `cost`. Team state from `TeamCreate` is not tracked here. The new active-teams.json is a parallel state mechanism. | Risk: LOW | Why: Not directly affected; confirms that dispatch_state.db is not a source of active team state and cannot be used as a substitute for the new PreCompact mechanism.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 Plugin manifest. No hooks key; hooks are auto-discovered from `hooks/hooks.json`. New hook scripts will be auto-discovered without changes to plugin.json, but the version will be bumped by pre-commit when any plugin file changes. | Risk: LOW | Why: No structural change needed; version bump is automatic.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/SKILL.md` \u2014 Documents the monitoring pattern using `monitor.py health` for inspecting native team state. The kage-bunshin skill covers `TeamCreate` health inspection; after this fix, it may need to note that team state is also persisted to `active-teams.json` before compaction. | Risk: LOW | Why: Content may become inconsistent with the new state model if not updated.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- No test files found for any hook scripts in `plugins/development-harness/hooks/` or `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/`. The existing hook scripts include inline test commands in their header comments (e.g., `echo '{...}' | node ./hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs`) but no automated pytest or Jest coverage. | Risk: HIGH | Why: There is no automated test harness for the hooks layer. The new PreCompact hook script, the TeammateIdle hook, and any SessionStart/PostCompact restoration hook will ship with no test coverage for their happy path, failure path, or idempotency behavior. End-to-end acceptance criteria require a \\\"spawn 3 teammates \u2192 force compact \u2192 verify compact includes team state \u2192 verify orchestrator resumes\\\" test sequence that does not currently have a test framework to run it in.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` directory exists but contains no hook-related test files. The `pyproject.toml` dev dependencies include `pytest`, `pytest-asyncio`, and `pytest-mock`, so the infrastructure for writing hook tests exists. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: The test framework exists but tests are missing; new hook scripts should have at minimum subprocess-based integration tests covering the stdin JSON schema and state file write/read cycle.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 The project CLAUDE.md instructs the orchestrator on session-start behavior and parallel execution rules (`TeamCreate` directive on line 103). There is no compact instructions section. The item description notes this is insufficient: \\\"The compact instructions in CLAUDE.md are insufficient on their own.\\\" This file will need a compact-awareness section once the hook mechanism is operational, to describe what the orchestrator should do after reading `bd prime` output at SessionStart. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: CLAUDE.md is loaded into every session and governs orchestrator behavior; without updated compact instructions, the orchestrator may not act on the injected state even when the hooks fire correctly.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 Plugin CLAUDE.md describes the harness workflow, SAM pipeline, and hooks architecture. The section on State Management and the Dispatch Orchestration System does not mention team state persistence across compaction. After this fix ships, the hooks integration section will need to document the new PreCompact/TeammateIdle/SessionStart lifecycle. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: AI agents loading this file will not know about the new state mechanism; they may fail to write team state after TeamCreate or fail to read it after restoration.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` \u2014 Instructs orchestrators to create teams, relay discoveries, and synthesize results. Does not mention compaction risks or the team state persistence requirement. Will need a \\\"Compaction Resilience\\\" section that tells the orchestrator to write team state to beads after TeamCreate. | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is the primary agent-facing instruction for all team spawning; if it does not instruct the orchestrator to persist team state, the orchestrator will not do so regardless of whether the hooks are wired.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/plan.md` \u2014 Work step 4.5 dispatches the team via `add-new-feature`. If `work-backlog-item` is the other primary entry point for TeamCreate, post-team state write may need to be documented here as well as in dispatch.md. | Risk: LOW | Why: May need a note; the primary change is in dispatch.md and work-backlog-item SKILL.md, not in the nested plan reference.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Section 6 \\\"Hook Trigger Conditions\\\" enumerates current hooks. After this item ships, PreCompact and TeammateIdle hooks will exist and need to be represented in the hook trigger table. | Risk: LOW | Why: Documentation drift \u2014 the diagram will be stale after new hooks are added, potentially misleading agents that load it to understand the hook landscape.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` \u2014 Describes hook integration table (SubagentStop, PostToolUse). The new TeammateIdle hook follows the same pattern and should be represented in this documentation for operators configuring the hook layer. | Risk: LOW | Why: Stale hook reference table after addition of new events.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 Central configuration file that must receive new entries for `PreCompact` (team state writer) and `TeammateIdle` (teammate completion tracker). No existing PreCompact or TeammateIdle entries are present. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Without entries in this file, no hook scripts will fire for these events regardless of script correctness. This is the single most critical configuration change in the entire item.\\n\\n- No `.github/workflows/` CI files were found for the development-harness plugin. The plugin does not have automated CI that runs hook tests. The acceptance criteria require an end-to-end verification sequence (spawn \u2192 compact \u2192 verify \u2192 resume) which has no CI harness to run it. | Risk: HIGH | Why: All quality gates for this feature must be manual at launch; automated regression protection does not exist for the hook layer.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` \u2014 Primary skill that tells the orchestrator how to use `TeamCreate`. After this fix, the dispatch skill must instruct orchestrators to call the beads state-write step immediately after `TeamCreate` succeeds. Without this agent instruction, the orchestrator will spawn teams without recording state, making the PreCompact hook produce empty output. | Risk: HIGH | Why: If the agent instruction does not change, hook wiring is useless \u2014 the state will never be written because the AI will not know to write it.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 Instructs the orchestrator on the full work pipeline. The step where teams are spawned for parallel implementation must include a post-spawn state-write directive. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Same as dispatch.md \u2014 the agent instruction must be updated or the PreCompact hook has nothing to persist.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/SKILL.md` \u2014 Covers monitoring via `monitor.py health` for native team health inspection. The kage-bunshin skill should note that native TeamCreate sessions (as opposed to tmux-based kage-bunshin sessions) are persisted to `active-teams.json`; the two monitoring paths serve different session types. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Agent confusion risk \u2014 the skill may be loaded to diagnose team state problems, and it currently does not distinguish between native team sessions (TeamCreate) and tmux sessions (kage-bunshin spawn.py). Without a note, the agent may try to use `monitor.py` for native team sessions where it is ineffective.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs` \u2014 Existing SessionStart hook that uses `hookSpecificOutput` to inject session ID. A new PostCompact or SessionStart hook that injects team state must follow this same output schema. The hook is the authoritative reference for how `hookSpecificOutput` is used in this plugin. | Risk: LOW | Why: Not a content-update risk but a pattern-precedent \u2014 new hooks must match this schema.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` | Role: configuration | Connection: Registration point for all hook events; must receive PreCompact and TeammateIdle entries for this fix | Action: CONFIG_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs` | Role: producer | Connection: Existing SessionStart hook; pattern precedent for hookSpecificOutput team-state restoration | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs` | Role: consumer | Connection: Reads kage-bunshin registry; does not cover native TeamCreate sessions; gap exposed by this fix | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs` | Role: consumer | Connection: Reads kage-bunshin registry on TaskCompleted; same coverage gap for native teams | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-end-kage-bunshin-cleanup.cjs` | Role: consumer | Connection: SessionEnd cleanup; will not clean up native TeamCreate sessions | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-child-notify.cjs` | Role: other-reference | Connection: Child-session notification writer; pattern reference for notification file approach | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-end-kage-bunshin-child-notify.cjs` | Role: other-reference | Connection: Child-session session_end writer; pattern reference | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-context-direct-writes.cjs` | Role: other-reference | Connection: PreToolUse Bash hook; the new PreCompact hook must not trigger this pattern (it writes to state/, not context/) | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` | Role: other-reference | Connection: PostToolUse/SubagentStop hook; pattern precedent for Python hook reading dh_paths | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` | Role: producer | Connection: Provides all DH state path resolution including DH_STATE_HOME override; new hooks must use this module for state/ path resolution | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py` | Role: other-reference | Connection: Confirmed no team/teammate tracking fields; active-teams.json is a separate parallel state file | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: Orchestrates TeamCreate; must add bd state-write step after team spawn | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: Primary TeamCreate usage pattern for all parallel dispatch; must add compaction resilience instructions | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: Monitoring docs; must distinguish native TeamCreate sessions from tmux kage-bunshin sessions in state tracking | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Hook integration table; will be stale after new TeammateIdle hook is added | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Section 6 hook trigger table; will not reflect new PreCompact/TeammateIdle entries | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Plugin architecture docs; no compaction-resilience section exists | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Project-level instructions; no compact instructions section; orchestrator behavior after restoration must be documented here | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` | Role: configuration | Connection: Auto-discovers hooks from hooks/hooks.json; version will be bumped by pre-commit | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 Zero entries for PreCompact or TeammateIdle; hook scripts cannot fire without registration here\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` \u2014 Primary agent instruction for TeamCreate; if it does not tell the orchestrator to write team state after spawning, the PreCompact hook has nothing to persist\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` \u2014 All state path resolution flows through here; new hooks that bypass it will silently break when DH_STATE_HOME is set\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - scope: Native TeamCreate sessions are invisible to all existing hook infrastructure (kage-bunshin registry, stop hook, task-completed hook, session-end cleanup); this item exposes a systemic gap, not just a missing hook\\n  - verification: No automated test coverage for any hook scripts; end-to-end acceptance criteria require a test sequence (spawn \u2192 compact \u2192 verify \u2192 resume) with no existing harness\\n  - agent-instruction: Both dispatch.md and work-backlog-item SKILL.md must be updated or the state-write step will never execute; hook wiring alone is insufficient\\n  - documentation: CLAUDE.md (project root) and plugin CLAUDE.md have no compaction-awareness content; restored orchestrators will not know how to act on injected state\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - Discovery: All existing kage-bunshin hook infrastructure is scoped to tmux-based sessions (registry-{session_id}.json). Native Claude Code `TeamCreate` sessions are architecturally separate and currently tracked by none of these hooks. This item's fix does not address the stop/cleanup gap for native teams; that is a follow-up scope risk if not explicitly addressed in the implementation plan.\\n  - The `bd` CLI (beads) dependency is required by the acceptance criteria (`bd update`, `bd prime`). Issue #1071 must ship first. Any implementation plan must declare this dependency and verify `bd` is on PATH before writing hook scripts that invoke it.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved (native TeamCreate vs kage-bunshin tmux session gap)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked (dh_paths.py DH_STATE_HOME, bd CLI dependency from #1071)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-25T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: orchestrator loses active team state across context compaction** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-25T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed session 2026-03-25: vm-flightsimulator orchestrator spawned 9 teammates, hit compaction, abandoned all of them\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-25)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Start a Claude Code session and load the `/dh:work-backlog-item` or `/dh:dispatch` skill.\\n2. Use `TeamCreate` to spawn 3 or more teammates with distinct tasks.\\n3. Continue the session until Claude Code triggers context compaction (either manually via `/compact` or naturally by filling the context window).\\n4. After compaction completes, observe the orchestrator's behavior: does it acknowledge the still-running teammates, wait for results, or send shutdown signals?\\n\\n**Observed result**: After compaction, the orchestrator does not reference the previously spawned team. Teammates continue running or idle without acknowledgment. The session ends with orphaned agents still alive.\\n\\n**Confirmed instance**: vm-flightsimulator session (2026-03-25) \u2014 9 teammates spawned, compaction fired, all abandoned.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 This is a data-loss bug in a core workflow. Any session that uses `TeamCreate` for parallel work and runs long enough to trigger compaction silently loses all team state. The orchestrator does not recover, teammates are abandoned, and results are lost. The failure is silent \u2014 the user has no indication work was abandoned. Affects the primary parallel-execution pattern (`/dh:dispatch`, `/dh:work-backlog-item`) that the entire development harness is designed around. Impact confirmed by observed production failure (9 orphaned agents, 2026-03-25). Ranked P1 rather than P0 because the failure requires a long session to trigger and does not corrupt persisted data \u2014 it loses in-flight work only.\\n\\nEffort: Medium-High\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Every workflow that uses `TeamCreate` for parallel agent dispatch in long sessions \u2014 `/dh:dispatch`, `/dh:work-backlog-item`, `/dh:add-new-feature`. Any task requiring more than a few thousand tokens of context is at risk.\\n- Bottleneck: Context compaction is automatic and unavoidable for long or complex sessions. The longer the session, the higher the probability of compaction, meaning complex multi-team tasks are disproportionately affected.\\n- Scope: All existing kage-bunshin hook infrastructure (stop, cleanup, task-completed) is scoped to tmux-based sessions and is blind to native `TeamCreate` sessions. There is no fallback mechanism. The failure is complete \u2014 no partial recovery is possible without this fix.\\n- Silent failure: The orchestrator does not report the loss. Results from orphaned teammates are not collected. If teammates produce artifacts, those artifacts exist but are never synthesized.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Long-running parallel sessions become viable: orchestrators can safely spawn teams knowing state will survive compaction.\\n- Teammate results are always collected: the orchestrator resumes awareness after compaction and either waits for pending teammates or sends shutdown signals as appropriate.\\n- Unblocks complex multi-team workflows: tasks currently too large to complete in a single context window can use parallel dispatch with confidence.\\n- Closes the systemic visibility gap for native `TeamCreate` sessions in the hook infrastructure: hooks will now be aware of native team sessions, not just kage-bunshin tmux sessions.\\n- Enables reliable end-to-end verification of the SAM pipeline for large milestones that require multiple context windows.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen context compaction fires during a session that has active teammates:\\n\\n1. Before compaction completes, the active team state (teammate names, team identifiers, task summaries) is written to a durable state file at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/active-teams.json`.\\n2. After compaction, when the session resumes (at SessionStart), the orchestrator is reminded of the active teams via a context injection \u2014 the names and tasks of still-running teammates appear in the context window.\\n3. The orchestrator resumes appropriate behavior: waiting for pending teammates, collecting their results, or sending shutdown signals.\\n4. When each teammate goes idle, a TeammateIdle hook fires and updates the persisted state to reflect that teammate's completion.\\n5. When all teammates have gone idle, the state file reflects a teams-complete status.\\n\\nThe orchestrator's awareness of active teams is never permanently lost due to compaction alone.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. After `TeamCreate` spawns teammates, a file exists at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/active-teams.json` containing the active team identifiers and task summaries. Verifiable: `cat ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/active-teams.json` shows non-empty team entries.\\n2. When context compaction fires (auto or manual), the `active-teams.json` file is updated before compaction completes. Verifiable: file mtime advances during the compaction event; file content is non-empty after compaction.\\n3. At the next SessionStart after compaction, the active-teams state is injected into context. Verifiable: the orchestrator's first response after resumption references the pending teammates by name or task.\\n4. When a teammate goes idle, the `active-teams.json` file is updated to reflect that teammate's completion. Verifiable: reading the file after a TeammateIdle event shows the affected teammate marked complete.\\n5. When all teammates have gone idle, the `active-teams.json` file reflects a fully-complete state (no pending teammates). Verifiable: `cat ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/active-teams.json` shows all entries complete or the file is cleared.\\n6. The state file path respects `DH_STATE_HOME` if set. Verifiable: set `DH_STATE_HOME=/tmp/dh-test` before running, confirm file appears at `/tmp/dh-test/projects/{slug}/state/active-teams.json`.\\n7. The hooks.json file contains entries for `PreCompact` and `TeammateIdle` events. Verifiable: `cat plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` shows both event names present.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-core-reference \u2014 authoritative hook event table; confirms PreCompact, TeammateIdle, SessionStart events and their output behavior |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-guide \u2014 hook output handling per event; confirms SessionStart injects into context, PostCompact does not |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-io-api \u2014 hook input/output schema for hookSpecificOutput pattern |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hook-creator \u2014 for creating new PreCompact and TeammateIdle hook scripts |\\n| Skill | /dh:dispatch \u2014 primary skill that uses TeamCreate; must be updated |\\n| Skill | /dh:kage-bunshin \u2014 monitoring docs; must be updated to distinguish session types |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs` \u2014 existing SessionStart hook using hookSpecificOutput; authoritative pattern reference |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs` \u2014 existing Stop hook reading registry; shows pattern for state-file-driven hook behavior |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` \u2014 existing state path resolution module; new hooks must extend this |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 PostToolUse/SubagentStop hook; pattern precedent for Python hook using dh_paths |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**HIGH risk \u2014 must change:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 no PreCompact or TeammateIdle entries; hooks cannot fire without registration here\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` \u2014 needs `state_dir()` accessor; all hooks must use this for `DH_STATE_HOME` compatibility\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` \u2014 primary agent instruction for TeamCreate; must include post-spawn state-write directive\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 origination point for TeamCreate invocations; must add state-write step after team spawn\\n\\n**MEDIUM risk \u2014 must verify or update:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs` \u2014 pattern precedent for `hookSpecificOutput`; new SessionStart hook must follow this schema\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs` \u2014 gap exposed: blind to native TeamCreate sessions; verify compatible with new state file\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs` \u2014 same gap; verify compatible\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-end-kage-bunshin-cleanup.cjs` \u2014 will not clean up native team sessions; verify compatible\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/SKILL.md` \u2014 must distinguish native TeamCreate sessions from tmux sessions\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 no compaction-resilience section; needs update after fix ships\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 no compact instructions section; needs update once hook mechanism is operational\\n\\n**LOW risk \u2014 content update after ship:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` \u2014 hook integration table will be stale\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Section 6 hook trigger table will be stale\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/plan.md` \u2014 may need a compaction-resilience note\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py` \u2014 read-only reference; confirms no team tracking fields (not a change target)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 version bumped automatically by pre-commit\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: `TeammateIdle` hook event \u2014 confirmed available in Claude Code hooks docs (VERIFIED by fact-check wave); no external dependency required\\n- Depends on: `PreCompact` hook event \u2014 confirmed available (VERIFIED); no external dependency required\\n- Depends on: `SessionStart` hook with `hookSpecificOutput` capability \u2014 confirmed available via existing `session-start-session-id.cjs` pattern (VERIFIED)\\n- Depends on: `dh_paths.py` `state_dir()` accessor \u2014 currently DERIVABLE; must be added before hook scripts can write to the correct path with DH_STATE_HOME support\\n- Does NOT depend on: beads (`bd`) CLI \u2014 REFUTED as a viable path; `bd` is not on PATH despite #1071 being closed; implementation must use direct file write approach, not beads\\n- Blocks: SAM planning phase for this item (cannot plan without groomed state)\\n- Blocks: any implementation that writes team state, as `dh_paths.py` must be extended first\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium-High \u2014 The hook mechanism itself (PreCompact write + SessionStart inject) is a contained change following established patterns (session-start-session-id.cjs is a direct precedent). However, the scope is broader than two hook scripts:\\n\\n- `dh_paths.py` needs a new `state_dir()` accessor\\n- `hooks.json` needs two new event registrations\\n- Two new hook scripts (PreCompact writer, TeammateIdle updater)\\n- One new or extended SessionStart hook (team-state injector)\\n- Two skill files updated with post-spawn state-write directives (`dispatch/SKILL.md`, `work-backlog-item/SKILL.md`)\\n- Three documentation files updated (`CLAUDE.md` project, `CLAUDE.md` plugin, `kage-bunshin/SKILL.md`)\\n- No existing automated test harness for hooks; integration tests for the new hooks must be written from scratch\\n\\nThe main complexity is that hook wiring alone is insufficient \u2014 agent instruction files must also be updated or the orchestrator will never write state in the first place. The absence of a test harness for the hooks layer adds friction to verification. End-to-end testing (spawn \u2192 compact \u2192 verify \u2192 resume) requires a real session and cannot be automated without a new test fixture.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: ALIGNED\\n**Rationale**: The fix restores intended behavior \u2014 orchestrators should maintain awareness of spawned teams across context boundaries. The development-harness design intent (stateless handoff via artifacts, session resilience) explicitly supports this. No divergence from product mission.\\n**Mission Statement Reference**: Development Harness design principle: every stage produces a named artifact stored for stateless handoff. Team state loss breaks this principle.\\n**Merged PR Evidence**: N/A \u2014 defect fix restoring designed behavior\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nThree change areas:\\n\\n**1. work-backlog-item skill** \u2014 after TeamCreate, add a step:\\n```\\nbd update <current-task-id> --notes \\\"Active teams: [teammate-name: task-summary, ...]\\\"\\n```\\nAnd after all teammates complete:\\n```\\nbd update <current-task-id> --notes \\\"Teams complete. Results collected.\\\"\\n```\\n\\n**2. TeammateIdle hook** \u2014 new hook in `plugins/development-harness/hooks/`:\\n```javascript\\n// teammate-idle-beads-sync.cjs\\n// Reads teammate_name and team_name from stdin\\n// Runs: bd update <current-task> --notes \\\"Teammate <name> idle/complete\\\"\\n// On last teammate: updates task status\\n```\\n\\n**3. PreCompact/SessionStart hooks** \u2014 already handled by `bd prime --stealth` wired via #1071 bootstrap.\\n\\nThe current-task-id needs to be discoverable at hook time. Options:\\n- Write it to `.beads/.current-task` when work-backlog-item starts\\n- Use `bd list --status=in_progress --json` to find the active task at hook time\\n\\nThe second option is more robust \u2014 no file to manage.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n**Rationale**: Traceable failure \u2014 TeamCreate spawns teammates, compaction fires, no state persistence mechanism exists, teammates become orphaned. Each cause is identifiable.\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys\\n**Scenario Target**: Orchestrator spawns team \u2192 compaction \u2192 team state lost \u2192 orphaned agents \u2192 missing results\\n\\n## Internal Contradictions Surfaced\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe item is not self-consistent. These contradictions are blocking-level gaps:\\n\\n1. bd REFUTED vs Implementation Notes: Dependencies section says \\\"Does NOT depend on: beads (bd) CLI \u2014 REFUTED.\\\" Implementation Notes still contain three concrete bd invocations: `bd update <current-task-id>` after TeamCreate, `bd update` in TeammateIdle hook, `bd prime --stealth` in SessionStart. These are mutually contradictory. No replacement mechanism is named.\\n\\n2. Prior RT-ICA Condition 9 incorrect: Marked \\\"AVAILABLE \u2014 dh_paths.py exposes state_dir()\\\". Verified from source: no state_dir() function exists in dh_paths.py. state_root() exists and returns ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/. The required state_dir() subdirectory accessor does not exist.\\n\\n3. Prior RT-ICA Condition 8 incorrect: Marked DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE for \\\"Runtime mechanism to query active team state at PreCompact time (dispatch_state.db)\\\". Impact Radius confirms dispatch_state.py schema has no team/teammate columns. The db cannot answer a team-state query.\\n\\n4. PostCompact appears in item description as a \\\"candidate\\\" despite Fact-check Claim 5 refuting it (debug-only output, no context injection). Design must explicitly close this path.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Conditions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. State file schema | Requires: JSON shape of active-teams.json \u2014 field names, status enum, multi-team structure, what \\\"fully complete\\\" looks like | Why: All 7 ACs reference the file; no schema is defined anywhere in the item.\\n\\n2. Discovery mechanism at PreCompact time | Requires: What writes active-teams.json at TeamCreate time and how PreCompact hook reads or re-persists it, given bd is refuted | Why: PreCompact hook has nothing to persist unless something wrote the file first.\\n\\n3. TeammateIdle hook stdin schema | Requires: Exact JSON fields Claude Code delivers to a TeammateIdle hook (team_name? teammate_name? session_id?) | Why: Hook must parse stdin to mark the correct teammate complete.\\n\\n4. Hook implementation language | Requires: CJS or Python (uv run --script) for new scripts | Why: CJS hooks cannot import dh_paths.py; Python hooks can. Choice determines slug derivation approach.\\n\\n5. state_dir() accessor | Requires: New function added to dh_paths.py returning ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/ | Why: Verified missing. All new hooks must use it for DH_STATE_HOME compatibility.\\n\\n6. bd replacement implementation | Requires: Concrete mechanism replacing all three bd references in Implementation Notes | Why: bd is refuted; no replacement is specified; implementation cannot start without it.\\n\\n7. AC #5 ambiguity | Requires: One observable outcome when all teammates idle \u2014 file cleared OR file shows all-complete status (not both) | Why: Behavioral test cannot verify an ambiguous acceptance criterion.\\n\\n8. Test approach | Requires: Specified behavioral test approach before implementation | Why: No hook test harness exists; repo rule (feedback_no_close_without_test) prohibits closing without behavioral test.\\n\\n9. PostCompact confirmed dead | AVAILABLE \u2014 Fact-check Claim 5 refuted PostCompact (debug-only output per hooks-guide line 195). SessionStart is the correct injection mechanism.\\n\\n10. dispatch_state.db unviable | AVAILABLE \u2014 Impact Radius confirms schema has no team/teammate columns. Not a usable team-state source.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Condition 1 (State file schema): MISSING \u2014 No schema defined in any section.\\n- Condition 2 (Discovery at PreCompact time): MISSING \u2014 bd refuted; \\\"direct file write approach\\\" named but mechanism unspecified.\\n- Condition 3 (TeammateIdle stdin schema): MISSING \u2014 hooks-io-api skill may have this; not present in item.\\n- Condition 4 (Hook language): DERIVABLE \u2014 Both CJS and Python precedents exist; choice not forced; must be stated.\\n- Condition 5 (state_dir() missing): MISSING \u2014 Verified from dh_paths.py source: function does not exist.\\n- Condition 6 (bd replacement): MISSING \u2014 Three bd calls in Implementation Notes, zero replacements.\\n- Condition 7 (AC #5 ambiguity): MISSING \u2014 \\\"file cleared OR all entries complete\\\" are different observable outcomes.\\n- Condition 8 (Test approach): MISSING \u2014 No test approach specified; risk summary calls this HIGH.\\n- Condition 9 (PostCompact dead): AVAILABLE \u2014 Fact-check Claim 5 PARTIALLY REFUTED; PostCompact output is debug-only.\\n- Condition 10 (dispatch_state.db unviable): AVAILABLE \u2014 Impact Radius Code Other References confirms no team columns.\\n\\nAVAILABLE: 2\\nDERIVABLE: 1\\nMISSING: 7\\n\\nDecision: BLOCKED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Missing Inputs Requested\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSchema:\\n- What is the JSON schema for active-teams.json?\\n  - Top-level structure (object keyed by team_id? array of entries?)\\n  - Required fields per team entry (team_id, teammate_name, task_summary, status...)\\n  - Status enum values (pending, idle, complete...)\\n  - Observable \\\"fully complete\\\" state (all status=complete? file deleted? top-level flag?)\\n  (Resolves Conditions 1 and 7 together)\\n\\nImplementation Mechanism (replacing bd):\\n- What triggers the active-teams.json write at TeamCreate time?\\n  (orchestrator skill directive? a hook event? something else?)\\n- Does the PreCompact hook re-read an already-written file, or query a live source?\\n- What replaces `bd prime --stealth` at SessionStart for injecting team state into context?\\n  (Resolves Conditions 2 and 6 together)\\n\\nHook API:\\n- What JSON fields does Claude Code deliver to a TeammateIdle hook via stdin?\\n  (Check /plugin-creator:hooks-io-api or hooks-guide references/claude-code.md)\\n  If undocumented, the test strategy must cover live-observation discovery before the script is written.\\n  (Resolves Condition 3)\\n\\nHook Language:\\n- Should new hook scripts follow CJS (session-start-session-id.cjs) or Python uv run --script (task_status_hook.py)?\\n  CJS: must reimplement slug derivation in JS. Python: can import dh_paths directly.\\n  (Resolves Condition 4)\\n\\nTest Approach:\\n- Minimum behavioral test before close. Options:\\n  a. Inline test commands in hook header (matching existing stop-kage-bunshin pattern) \u2014 manual only\\n  b. pytest integration tests in plugins/development-harness/tests/ with mocked stdin JSON\\n  c. End-to-end test fixture: real session, spawn, compact, verify\\n  Pick one before implementation starts. (Resolves Condition 8)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"15518ce0f4b573b6d25c5231df71500170487996b7ed0310d1d836527e69b623\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCQDXA\"}"}